[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-23638"] :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nWe now simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-23847/selection/046bb4f82b3b17b27cef0f3244736e00142ec6fa92bd6221752b1ee615aa34df" :answer/id #uuid "95a465c7-293d-5868-9729-6d9890245f71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23847/selection/ff8f1ffdc2cbfb1a4a64c41b9ac9f0be14fabc5b524807351f2d1cd1f9f0e487" :answer/id #uuid "305720db-2395-5b37-9efc-08925417afba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23847/selection/29be3cf1aa7619e3ab92ed63e9016b4012bc96ee45049581d3b9397c2783490c" :answer/id #uuid "51c5b52b-4f84-5bc6-9101-daf5f31ba07b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23847/selection/ea1e338de2a0cb8a640a44950398210d1ca222223a655996523a7e9a1815ad8e" :answer/id #uuid "d1e1c755-e4ff-5792-b133-68632c93126e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23847/selection/7048515d8d03871e88488698b26c9b226ee04b8b8095a0a53e3c45f7964a4c43" :answer/id #uuid "f513e813-c83c-5d0e-aada-553dba8bb45b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23847/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "485bc948-a7fc-5258-b91b-e1fa821057bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-23847/selection/ea1e338de2a0cb8a640a44950398210d1ca222223a655996523a7e9a1815ad8e" :answer-field/choices ["q-23847/selection/046bb4f82b3b17b27cef0f3244736e00142ec6fa92bd6221752b1ee615aa34df" "q-23847/selection/ff8f1ffdc2cbfb1a4a64c41b9ac9f0be14fabc5b524807351f2d1cd1f9f0e487" "q-23847/selection/29be3cf1aa7619e3ab92ed63e9016b4012bc96ee45049581d3b9397c2783490c" "q-23847/selection/ea1e338de2a0cb8a640a44950398210d1ca222223a655996523a7e9a1815ad8e" "q-23847/selection/7048515d8d03871e88488698b26c9b226ee04b8b8095a0a53e3c45f7964a4c43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-23847" :question/id #uuid "25be672b-a303-5e5c-b0b8-1502311a3b23" :question/math-academy-id "q-23847" :question/problem "$({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+{tan}^{2}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nAlso, recall the Pythagorean formula for sines and cosines:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above identities, we can simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+{tan}^{2}⁡x & =1+{tan}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-23847/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-23847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-65397"] :question/problem "${sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x & =1+{tan}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x=1-{tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-120637/selection/1af7e13befc2d99c990cb25ccaed11b73211adacccdeb3d96a12ee4830dd54b2" :answer/id #uuid "f40b34e7-28c4-5463-9c46-3d1cbe83b31b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120637/selection/fbdfea5b1daf4d74b7704516814c3c28369f5bc5063ac90d7a612b0fa0bb5de8" :answer/id #uuid "5211dc81-c47c-5e7a-aec2-7e7ef01f180b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120637/selection/658c7ed62daa9d79a1130454391674f14bd5e0f2eb9656af04617f2a96060246" :answer/id #uuid "2aa944d8-fb13-551d-8014-09374f4476c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120637/selection/19599ec0b6f7be72ec48d28a49c620e3a67678a08c03ad5cebd5e852c084720f" :answer/id #uuid "ccc1744f-9c88-5904-b07b-2820f703c892" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120637/selection/a0332b537f4486805ad1793740b0a1ac4165eaeb48e40facdc78c5de1981c15a" :answer/id #uuid "51700ef9-973c-50f4-b670-ac61225b1849" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120637/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a30eec5-02ab-573d-964c-df9797724c13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120637/selection/1af7e13befc2d99c990cb25ccaed11b73211adacccdeb3d96a12ee4830dd54b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-120637/selection/1af7e13befc2d99c990cb25ccaed11b73211adacccdeb3d96a12ee4830dd54b2" "q-120637/selection/fbdfea5b1daf4d74b7704516814c3c28369f5bc5063ac90d7a612b0fa0bb5de8" "q-120637/selection/658c7ed62daa9d79a1130454391674f14bd5e0f2eb9656af04617f2a96060246" "q-120637/selection/19599ec0b6f7be72ec48d28a49c620e3a67678a08c03ad5cebd5e852c084720f" "q-120637/selection/a0332b537f4486805ad1793740b0a1ac4165eaeb48e40facdc78c5de1981c15a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120637" :question/id #uuid "88ef7ccf-542e-5c42-b011-ca1cd5a37425" :question/math-academy-id "q-120637" :question/problem "${tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1+{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1+{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1+1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1+{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta =2{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120637/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640012b-79f9-5f6b-a26b-a7f4fe8c0e7b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142820/selection/2d8e76e38802e8b4996a73378f7ac9c3369b1a21338db67149215a9d20fd2cee" :answer/id #uuid "09c5177a-02dc-53ca-b632-5ad35b640806" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142820/selection/7048515d8d03871e88488698b26c9b226ee04b8b8095a0a53e3c45f7964a4c43" :answer/id #uuid "c12249f7-5cc9-5a01-ad57-f69901aaa404" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142820/selection/ea1e338de2a0cb8a640a44950398210d1ca222223a655996523a7e9a1815ad8e" :answer/id #uuid "7cdb692a-1c41-5c58-a41a-d433b0ebb85f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142820/selection/1a025743f7e4bc5b2cdf34f757ec457131137228b3a25c58a33251f3468807e6" :answer/id #uuid "d0dcfc5e-20f3-5b69-a71a-01b887306b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142820/selection/b6434e4e8ab785c46c004ce71c38ae3a0d284f339c304c108c12567c771f38e9" :answer/id #uuid "dd8241ec-9038-5558-96e5-6810f7b27dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142820/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4931d0d-9ccd-5f4d-be79-9fd5562d9f04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142820/selection/2d8e76e38802e8b4996a73378f7ac9c3369b1a21338db67149215a9d20fd2cee" :answer-field/choices ["q-142820/selection/2d8e76e38802e8b4996a73378f7ac9c3369b1a21338db67149215a9d20fd2cee" "q-142820/selection/7048515d8d03871e88488698b26c9b226ee04b8b8095a0a53e3c45f7964a4c43" "q-142820/selection/ea1e338de2a0cb8a640a44950398210d1ca222223a655996523a7e9a1815ad8e" "q-142820/selection/1a025743f7e4bc5b2cdf34f757ec457131137228b3a25c58a33251f3468807e6" "q-142820/selection/b6434e4e8ab785c46c004ce71c38ae3a0d284f339c304c108c12567c771f38e9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142820" :question/id #uuid "89c09b24-68b3-54af-bb86-2a4e34353860" :question/math-academy-id "q-142820" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)-{tan}^{2}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)-{tan}^{2}⁡x & ={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1+{tan}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142820/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640012b-79f9-5f6b-a26b-a7f4fe8c0e7b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142820"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
